cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "PILAR-2b: Plataforma Inteligente de Localização e Aproveitamento de Resíduos para Biogas e Bioprodutos"
version: "3.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-21"
license: GPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/aikiesan/Pilar-2b"
url: "https://cp2b.unicamp.br/pilar2b/pt-BR"
abstract: >
  PILAR-2b is an open-source web GIS platform for mapping the biogas and
  biomethane potential of agricultural, livestock and urban residues. It covers
  the 645 municipalities of São Paulo State, Brazil, with a beta pilot for
  Minas Gerais. It integrates public datasets (IBGE, MapBiomas, SNIS/SINISA,
  OpenStreetMap) into a PostGIS database served by a FastAPI backend and a
  Next.js interface, so the potential can be explored per municipality,
  substrate and scenario in a browser, without desktop GIS software.
